  "lem:383A": {
    "lean_file": "OpenMath/Chapter3/Section383.lean",
    "lean_symbol": "OpenMath.Chapter3.Section383.multiplicative_conv",
    "notes": "Cycle 078. Formalised via convolution product (eq 383a) on Multiset RootedTree. Required proving auxiliary Mathlib lemma _PowersetAdd.powerset_add (not in Mathlib). Forest := Multiset RootedTree; convolution defined via S.powerset; the (S+T).powerset = (S.powerset \u00d7\u02e2 T.powerset).map (\u00b7 + \u00b7) identity is the load-bearing combinatorial step. Axioms = [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. Non-vacuity witness: isMultiplicative_const_one.",
    "status": "formalized"
  },
  "lem:383B": {
    "lean_file": "OpenMath/Chapter3/Section383.lean",
    "lean_symbol": "OpenMath.Chapter3.Section383.convProduct_assoc",
    "notes": "Cycle 080. Convolution product associativity (\u03b1\u03b2)\u03b3 = \u03b1(\u03b2\u03b3). Stated WITHOUT IsMultiplicative hypotheses \u2014 a faithful generalisation, since the textbook proof uses only the algebraic structure of the convolution sum (not multiplicativity). Three private helper lemmas: convProduct_assoc_lhs_eq, convProduct_assoc_rhs_eq (LHS/RHS as double sums via Multiset.bind), and double_powerset_swap (the key combinatorial bijection (Q,T) \u2194 (Q+T,Q), proved by induction on S applying the IH thrice with reparameterised f). Closes via `S - Q - (R - Q) = S - R` for Q \u2264 R. Axioms = [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound].",
    "status": "formalized"
  },
  "lem:383C": {
    "lean_file": "OpenMath/Chapter3/Section383.lean",
    "lean_symbol": "OpenMath.Chapter3.Section383.exists_inverse_of_isMultiplicative",
    "notes": "Cycle 081. Existence of left/right inverses in G\u2081 (multiplicative forest mappings). Constructive: exhibits convInverse \u03b1 (closed form (-1)^|F| \u00b7 \u220f_{t \u2208 F} \u03b1({t})) as the explicit witness. Supporting infrastructure: convOne (identity element), isMultiplicative_convOne (identity is in G\u2081), convInverse_isMultiplicative (the closed form is multiplicative \u2014 no hypothesis on \u03b1 needed), convProduct_singleton_eq_zero / convProduct_singleton_symm_eq_zero (per-singleton zero), convProduct_convInverse / convProduct_convInverse_symm (right/left inverse property by Multiset.induction with multiplicativity). FAITHFULNESS CAVEAT: this proves inverse-existence for our convProduct (multiset sub-selection), not Butcher's convolution (vertex-subset partition). Inverse exists in both algebras; closed form differs (Butcher's involves partition sum, ours is product). See .prover-state/issues/convolution_vertex_vs_multiset.md. Axioms = [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound].",
    "status": "formalized"
  },
