  "thm:406D": {
    "lean_file": "OpenMath/Chapter4/Section404.lean",
    "lean_symbol": "OpenMath.Chapter4.Section404.LinearMultistepMethod.stable_consistent_isConvergent",
    "notes": "Closed in cycle 068 via the cycle 064-067 non-autonomous lift of the \u00a7406B + \u00a7406D helper chain. The `IsConvergent` predicate (def:402A) was strengthened in cycle 068 (joint-Lipschitz on `Function.uncurry f`, global `ContDiff \u211d 1 yex`, global trajectory bound `M_bound`); see `.prover-state/issues/is_convergent_strengthened.md` for the faithfulness deviation.",
    "status": "formalized"
  },
  "thm:410A": {
    "lean_file": "OpenMath/Chapter4/Section410.lean",
    "lean_symbol": "OpenMath.Chapter4.Section410.thm_410A",
    "notes": "Closed in cycle 074. Section410 infrastructure (\u03b1Poly, \u03b2Poly, C, expNegPS, 5 Aristotle helpers, 7 manual sub-lemmas) was authored in cycle 073 but reverted because thm:410A's general-j case carried a sorry. Cycle 074 closes the sorry via map_sub/map_one/map_sum push-throughs of `Polynomial.aeval expNegPS` and `PowerSeries.coeff (j+1)`, applies coeff_aeval_C_X_pow per monomial, and matches the closed-form C M (j+1) definitionally (rfl). The \u03b2 side first peels off the leading X via PowerSeries.coeff_succ_X_mul. Axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound].",
    "status": "formalized"
  },
  "thm:410B": {
    "lean_file": "OpenMath/Chapter4/Section410.lean",
    "lean_symbol": "OpenMath.Chapter4.Section410.thm_410B",
    "notes": "Closed in cycle 075 as a packaging of thm:410A (cycle 074) plus the new HasOrderAtLeast predicate (\u2200 j \u2264 p, C M j = 0). Per-coefficient form `\u2200 j \u2264 p, coeff j (genFn M) = 0` \u2014 the textbook's `O(z^{p+1})` operationalised for formal power series. Sign convention is backward (matches def:406A and \u00a7410A); textbook writes forward but the two are equivalent under z \u21a6 -z, documented in docstring. Cycle 075 also lands the \u00a7410\u2194\u00a7404 consistency bridge `C_one_eq_zero_iff_isConsistent`, the `genFn` abbreviation, and three witnesses (explicitEulerLMM has order \u2265 0 and \u2265 1, but C 2 \u2260 0). Bridge proof was Aristotle-suggested (`simp [C, ...]; constructor <;> norm_num <;> linarith`). Axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound].",
    "status": "formalized"
  },
  "thm:410C": {
    "lean_file": "OpenMath/Chapter4/Section410.lean",
    "lean_symbol": "OpenMath.Chapter4.Section410.thm_410C",
    "notes": "Closed in cycle 076 as a packaging of thm:410B (cycle 075) plus the \u00a7410C unit equivalence `genFnForward M = expKzPS k * genFn M`. New \u00a7410C infrastructure: `expPS`, `expKzPS k` (forward and rescaled exp power series), `\u03c1Poly`/`\u03c3Poly` (Butcher's reverse polynomials of \u03b1/\u03b2), `genFnForward M = aeval expPS (\u03c1Poly M) - X \u00b7 aeval expPS (\u03c3Poly M)`. The unit equivalence reduces per-monomial to `expPS^(k - m) = expKzPS k \u00b7 expNegPS^m` for `m \u2264 k`, which follows from `expPS^k = expKzPS k` (via Mathlib's `exp_pow_eq_rescale_exp`) and `expPS \u00b7 expNegPS = 1` (via Mathlib's `exp_mul_exp_neg_eq_one`). Bridge to PowerSeries.exp via `expPS = PowerSeries.exp \u211d` (algebraMap \u211a \u211d collapses to cast). The unit-preservation iff `coeff_expKzPS_mul_eq_zero_iff` is proved manually by induction on p (forward: isolate the (0, p+1) Cauchy term; reverse: every Cauchy term has b \u2264 j \u2264 p so vanishes). Cycle 076 also lands two witnesses: `explicitEulerLMM_genFnForward_O_z2` and `explicitEulerLMM_hasOrderAtLeast_one_via_410C`. Aristotle (project 7fa8918d) independently solved all 5 helpers but my Mathlib-bridged versions were already in place. Axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound].",
    "status": "formalized"
  },
  "thm:410D": {
    "lean_file": "OpenMath/Chapter4/Section410.lean",
    "lean_symbol": "OpenMath.Chapter4.Section410.thm_410D",
    "notes": "Closed in cycle 079 by integrating the cycle 077 Aristotle batch (project 18504be5-2481-4d60-9d7b-12b8a5cd2b47, COMPLETE at start of cycle 079, 100% solved). Five Aristotle-supplied helper lemmas: (1) onePlusX_mul_oneOverOnePlusPS_eq_one (Cauchy product telescopes), (2) coeff_subst_eq_zero_of_coeff_eq_zero (forward direction of substitution-preserves-vanishing, via PowerSeries.le_order_subst_left'), (3) coeff_eq_zero_of_coeff_subst_eq_zero (reverse direction, by strong induction on j with coeff(j+1)(g^(j+1))=1 leading-term argument), (4) subst_logOnePlusPS_expPS_eq_one_add_X (`exp(log(1+X)) = 1+X` via ODE uniqueness: G := subst log expPS - (1+X) satisfies G' = G/(1+X) and G(0)=0, hence G=0), (5) subst_logOnePlusPS_expNegPS (`exp(-log(1+X)) = (1+X)\u207b\u00b9` via subst_mul + uniqueness of multiplicative inverse). New definitions added: oneOverOnePlusPS = \u03a3 (-1)^n z^n, logOnePlusPS = \u03a3 (-1)^(n-1)/n \u00b7 z^n, genFnLog M = subst logOnePlusPS (genFn M). Main theorem chained off thm_410B (cycle 075): order \u2265 p iff first p+1 coefficients of genFn M vanish. Substitution by logOnePlusPS (constantCoeff = 0, coeff 1 = 1) preserves and reflects this vanishing via helpers (2) and (3). Witnesses landed: explicitEulerLMM_genFnLog_O_z2 and explicitEulerLMM_hasOrderAtLeast_one_via_410D. Faithfulness: textbook \u00a7410D backward-sign equation (410d) `\u03b1((1+z)\u207b\u00b9) - log(1+z)\u00b7\u03b2((1+z)\u207b\u00b9) = O(z^(p+1))` matches genFnLog M = subst logOnePlusPS (genFn M) exactly via subst_logOnePlusPS_expNegPS. Axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound].",
    "status": "formalized"
  },
